        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.124,
            0.414,
            0.143
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "While-Loops are Fundamental"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.154,
            0.449,
            0.172
          ],
          "content": "• They are behind all **long-running applications**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.173,
            0.359,
            0.189
          ],
          "content": "§ Always have a top level while loop"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.19,
            0.428,
            0.207
          ],
          "content": "§ And many subtasks are themselves while loops"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.21,
            0.434,
            0.227
          ],
          "content": "• The challenge is how these loops fit together"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.228,
            0.417,
            0.245
          ],
          "content": "§ Very often you are not writing all of the code"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.246,
            0.409,
            0.262
          ],
          "content": "§ Your code has to fit inside “invisible” loops"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.264,
            0.451,
            0.28
          ],
          "content": "§ Your code can cause an infinite loop you never saw"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.282,
            0.452,
            0.3
          ],
          "content": "• To understand this, we will look at a **case study**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.566,
            0.123,
            0.856,
            0.143
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "The Game of Pig: A Random Game"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.538,
            0.155,
            0.758,
            0.175
          ],
          "content": "• Play progresses clockwise"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.538,
            0.18,
            0.769,
            0.2
          ],
          "content": "• On your turn, throw the die:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.555,
            0.203,
            0.77,
            0.221
          ],
          "content": "§ If roll 1: lose turn, score zero"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.556,
            0.225,
            0.771,
            0.244
          ],
          "content": "§ Anything else: add it to score"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.575,
            0.245,
            0.764,
            0.263
          ],
          "content": "• Can also roll again (and lose)"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.778,
            0.185,
            0.864,
            0.259
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_0_image_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.525,
            0.331,
            0.539,
            0.346
          ],
          "content": "2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.574,
            0.264,
            0.741,
            0.283
          ],
          "content": "• If stop, score is “banked”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.13,
            0.405,
            0.446,
            0.425
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Advantage of Class-Based Applications"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.539,
            0.285,
            0.742,
            0.305
          ],
          "content": "• First person to 100 wins"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.435,
            0.411,
            0.452
          ],
          "content": "• **Function calls** correspond to **call frames**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.453,
            0.409,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": "§ Any work is lost when the game is complete"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.47,
            0.361,
            0.485
          ],
          "content": "§ What if you want to keep statistics?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.486,
            0.301,
            0.503
          ],
          "content": "• **Objects** live in the **heap**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.505,
            0.373,
            0.52
          ],
          "content": "§ Any attributes will continue to persist"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.52,
            0.394,
            0.536
          ],
          "content": "§ Still have functions (methods) to do stuff"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.538,
            0.401,
            0.555
          ],
          "content": "• **Idea**: **Refactor** our function-based apps"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.555,
            0.388,
            0.571
          ],
          "content": "§ Turn some local variables into attributes"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.571,
            0.398,
            0.588
          ],
          "content": "§ But not all – only those we want to “save”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.573,
            0.405,
            0.849,
            0.425
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Understanding a GUI Application"
        },
        {
